     then be identified via fstat(1).  That special file can then be mounted
     by mmoouunntt__ffuusseeffss.

     However, the procedure of spawning a daemon will usually be automated so
     that it is performed by mmoouunntt__ffuusseeffss.  If the command invoking a given
     _f_u_s_e___d_a_e_m_o_n is appended to the list of arguments, mmoouunntt__ffuusseeffss will call
     the _f_u_s_e___d_a_e_m_o_n via that command.  In that way the _f_u_s_e___d_a_e_m_o_n will be
     instructed to attach itself to _s_p_e_c_i_a_l.  From that on mounting goes as in
     the simple case. (See _D_A_E_M_O_N _M_O_U_N_T_S.)

     The _s_p_e_c_i_a_l argument will normally be treated as the path of the special
